          "text": "{\"regions\":{\"r2\":{\"type\":\"stanza_note\",\"lines\":[{\"n\":1,\"text\":\"\u0935\u094d\u092f\u0924\u093f\u0930\u0947\u0915\u0903 \u0938 \u090f\u0935 \u0938\u0903 \u0964 There is \u0935\u094d\u092f\u0966 when the superiority over the\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":2,\"text\":\"\u0909\u092a\u092e\u093e\u0928 ( the standard of comparison ) of what is different from\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":3,\"text\":\"it is mentioned, as that of \u0938\u0924\u093e\u0902 \u092a\u094d\u0930\u091c\u094d\u091e\u094b\u0928\u094d\u092e\u0947\u0937 over \u092d\u0942 &c., here.\",\"end\":\"space\"}],\"uncertain\":true,\"note\":\"Some Devanagari in the quotation is difficult to read.\"},\"r3\":{\"type\":\"stanza_note\",\"lines\":[{\"n\":1,\"text\":\"Sl. 11. The idea of the sl. is that one should make once\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":2,\"text\":\"for all a choice of the alternatives stated and act accordingly;\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":3,\"text\":\"\u092d\u093e\u0930\u094d\u092f\u093e\u2014\u092d\u094d\u0930\u093f\u092f\u0924\u0947 \u0907\u0924\u093f \u092d\u093e\u0930\u094d\u092f\u093e: fr. \u092d\u0943+\u092f ( \u0923\u094d\u092f\u0924\u094d, ) \u092d\u0930\u094d\u0924\u0941\u0902 \u092f\u094b\u0917\u094d\u092f\u093e \u0935\u093e; he should\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":4,\"text\":\"have the one or the other and nothing between these.\",\"end\":\"space\"}],\"uncertain\":true,\"note\":\"The grammatical abbreviation and Sanskrit phrase are difficult to read.\"},\"r4\":{\"type\":\"stanza_note\",\"lines\":[{\"n\":1,\"text\":\"Sl. 12. \u0915\u092e\u0920\u2014\u0915\u0947 \u091c\u0932\u0947 \u092e\u0920\u0924\u093f \u0907\u0924\u093f; aff. \u0905 ( \u0905\u091a\u094d ); a tortoise. Here\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":2,\"text\":\"the great Tortoise\u2014Vishnu\u2019s \u0915\u0942\u0930\u094d\u092e\u093e\u0935\u0924\u093e\u0930. \u0915\u0941\u0932\u093e\u091a\u0932\u2014Name of the\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":3,\"text\":\"seven principal mountain chains, for which see com. \u0926\u093f\u0917\u094d\u0917\u091c\u2014\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":4,\"text\":\"The elephants of the quarters, supporting and guarding them.\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":5,\"text\":\"The names are thus given by Amarasimha-\u0910\u0930\u093e\u0935\u0924\u0903 \u092a\u0941\u0923\u094d\u0921\u0930\u0940\u0915\u094b \u0935\u093e\u092e\u0928\u0903\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":6,\"text\":\"\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":7,\"text\":\"\u0915\u0941\u092e\u0941\u0926\u094b\u093d\u091e\u094d\u091c\u0928\u0903 \u0965 \u092a\u0941\u0937\u094d\u092a\u0926\u0928\u094d\u0924\u0903 \u0938\u093e\u0930\u094d\u0935\u092d\u094c\u092e\u0903 \u0938\u0941\u092a\u094d\u0930\u0924\u0940\u0915\u0936\u094d\u091a \u0926\u093f\u0917\u094d\u0917\u091c\u093e\u0903 \u0965 The R\u00e2m\u00e2yana\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":8,\"text\":\"gives them differently, viz. Virup\u00e2ksha for the East, Saumanasa\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":9,\"text\":\"for the West, Mah\u00e2padma for the South, and Bhadra for\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":10,\"text\":\"the North.\",\"end\":\"space\"}],\"uncertain\":true,\"note\":\"The Sanskrit etymology and names in the quotation are not entirely clear.\"},\"r5\":{\"type\":\"stanza_note\",\"lines\":[{\"n\":1,\"text\":\"\u092a\u094d\u0930\u0924\u093f\u092a\u0928\u094d\u0928\u2014what is undertaken. \u0905\u092e\u0932\u092e\u0928\u0938\u093e\u092e\u094d\u2014of those whose minds\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":2,\"text\":\"are pure, i. e. who never use equivocal language but state in\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":3,\"text\":\"unmistakable terms what they would do. It is not clear what\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":4,\"text\":\"the gist of the sl. is. The connection between strong-mind-\",\"end\":\"hyphen\"},{\"n\":5,\"text\":\"edness and amalamanasatva is not very clear. Probably the\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":6,\"text\":\"poet expresses here the same idea as he does in the last line\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":7,\"text\":\"of the next sloka. The fig. is \u0935\u094d\u092f\u0924\u093f\u0930\u0947\u0915,\",\"end\":\"space\"}],\"uncertain\":false,\"note\":null},\"r6\":{\"type\":\"stanza_note\",\"lines\":[{\"n\":1,\"text\":\"Sl. 12. \u0915\u0942\u0930\u094d\u092e\u0938\u094d\u092f\u2014\u0915\u094b \u091c\u0932\u0947 \u090a\u0930\u094d\u092e\u093f\u0903 \u0935\u0947\u0917\u094b \u0905\u0938\u094d\u092f \u0964 A tortoise. Here the se-\",\"end\":\"hyphen\"},{\"n\":2,\"text\":\"cond incarnation of Vishnu. Mr. Telang reads the third line as\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":3,\"text\":\"\u0915\u093f\u0902 \u0924\u094d\u0935\u0926\u094d\u0917\u0940\u0966\u2014\u0928 \u092e\u0928\u0938\u093e, suggesting that the line should be taken\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":4,\"text\":\"as a question and that for this it would be better to read \u0915\u093f\u0902 \u091a\u093e-\",\"end\":\"hyphen\"},{\"n\":5,\"text\":\"\u0919\u094d\u0917\u0940\u0915\u0943\u0924\u092e\u094d, and further remarks\u2014\u201cThe reading \u0915\u093f\u0902\u0924\u0941 is more appro-\",\"end\":\"hyphen\"},{\"n\":6,\"text\":\"priate to what I think is the intended sense, but to obtain that\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":7,\"text\":\"\u0928 must be got rid of.\u201d But the third line makes a general\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":8,\"text\":\"statement and supports the figure in the last line, while the\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":9,\"text\":\"questions in the first two lines refer to specific objects. \u0928\u093f\u0930\u094d\u0935\u093e\u0939\u0903\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":10,\"text\":\"&c.\u2014construe \u0938\u0924\u093e\u092e\u0947\u0924\u0926\u094d\u0927\u093f \u0917\u094b\u0924\u094d\u0930\u0935\u094d\u0930\u0924\u0902 ( \u092f\u0924\u094d ) \u092a\u094d\u0930\u0924\u093f\u092a\u0928\u094d\u0928\u0935\u0938\u094d\u0924\u0941\u0937\u0941 \u0928\u093f\u0930\u094d\u0935\u093e\u0939\u0903 \u0964 \u0935\u094d\u0930\u0924\u2014\",\"end\":\"space\"}],\"uncertain\":true,\"note\":\"Several Sanskrit words and abbreviations are difficult to read.\"},\"r1\":{\"type\":\"page_number\",\"lines\":[{\"n\":1,\"text\":\"( 46 )\",\"end\":\"space\"}],\"uncertain\":false,\"note\":null}},\"units\":[{\"id\":\"u1\",\"type\":\"notes\",\"number\":null,\"label\":null,\"open_start\":true,\"open_end\":true,\"children\":[\"u2\",\"u3\",\"u4\",\"u5\"]},{\"id\":\"u2\",\"type\":\"stanza_note\",\"number\":null,\"label\":null,\"open_start\":true,\"open_end\":false,\"children\":[\"r2\"]},{\"id\":\"u3\",\"type\":\"stanza_note\",\"number\":\"11\",\"label\":null,\"open_start\":false,\"open_end\":false,\"children\":[\"r3\"]},{\"id\":\"u4\",\"type\":\"stanza_note\",\"number\":\"12\",\"label\":null,\"open_start\":false,\"open_end\":false,\"children\":[\"r4\",\"r5\"]},{\"id\":\"u5\",\"type\":\"stanza_note\",\"number\":\"12\",\"label\":null,\"open_start\":false,\"open_end\":true,\"children\":[\"r6\"]}],\"flows\":[{\"flow\":\"main\",\"units\":[\"u1\"]}],\"relations\":[]}"
